<title>UK: Turkey tenders to buy 60-65 kt low sulphur fuel.</title>
<headline>Turkey tenders to buy 60-65 kt low sulphur fuel.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Turkey's state utility Tupras has issued a tender to buy 60-65,000 tonnes of low sulphur fuel oil in March, traders said.</p>
<p>The tender, which closes on March 5, calls for 30-35,000 tonnes to be delivered to Izmit between March 18-20, and 35,000 tonnes to be delivered to Izmir between March 20-25.</p>
<p>The fuel oil must contain a maximum of five parts per million asphaltenes.</p>
<p>-- London newsroom +44 171 542 8167</p>
</text>
